    "sbar": {
      "situation": "The bank payment journey has recovered. Two recovery checks in a row ran the main journey cleanly, the last at 21 s.",
      "background": "The pipeline changed payments max_transfer_minor from 1000000 to 1 about 14 s before diagnosis. It changed gateway balance_cache_ttl_s from 0.5 to 600.0 about 12 s before diagnosis.",
      "assessment": "The payments limit change made payments refuse nearly every transfer with '422 amount exceeds transfer limit' (confidence 0.97). The gateway cache change was a hidden second fault that would have shown stale balances for up to 10 minutes once payments worked (confidence 0.8). The incident commander reverted both settings itself, max_transfer_minor to 1000000 and balance_cache_ttl_s to 0.5, and both reverts succeeded.",
      "recommendation": "Find out why the pipeline pushed these two config values and block it from repeating them. Operations should review the payments refused with 422 during the incident, since customers may need to retry them."
    },
